Overseas patients care deeply about their rights during cross-border treatment. Our 5-layer patient rights protection system safeguards international patients throughout their care.
1. Transparent informed care: before treatment, fully explain the condition, options, expected outcomes, limitations, risks and estimated costs, without overstating benefits or concealing risks;
2. Complete medical documentation: all examination reports, surgical records and discharge summaries are issued and retained to international standards for follow-up at home and insurance claims;
3. Dedicated medical concierge: patients can raise questions and requests through their concierge for prompt coordination with the medical team;
4. Medical dispute mediation: an independent channel provides neutral mediation of disagreements during care, with a success rate of up to 82%;
5. Aftercare and follow-up: remote consultations and rehabilitation guidance after discharge, with continued monitoring of the patient's condition.
We cannot promise ideal outcomes for every treatment, but we ensure informed choice, complaint channels and comprehensive ongoing medical support.
Multiple safeguards help overseas patients in China have their concerns heard and their rights protected.

